<xmldoc><copyright>SAME AS NELSON SOFTWARE</copyright><language>fr_FR</language><keyword>idct</keyword><short_description>Transformation en cosinus discrete inverse.</short_description><syntax><syntax_item>X = idct(Y)</syntax_item><syntax_item>X = idct(Y, N)</syntax_item><syntax_item>X = idct(Y, N, DIM)</syntax_item></syntax><param_input><param_input_item><param_name>Y</param_name><param_description>coefficients de la transformation en cosinus discrete.</param_description></param_input_item><param_input_item><param_name>N</param_name><param_description>longueur de transformation : Y est complete par des zeros ou tronque a la longueur N.</param_description></param_input_item><param_input_item><param_name>DIM</param_name><param_description>dimension le long de laquelle operer.</param_description></param_input_item></param_input><param_output><param_output_item><param_name>X</param_name><param_description>signal reconstruit (inverse de la DCT-II orthonormale).</param_description></param_output_item></param_output><description><p><b>idct</b> calcule l&apos;inverse de la transformation en cosinus discrete de type II orthonormale le long de la premiere dimension non singleton par defaut. Pour les matrices, chaque colonne est transformee independamment.</p></description><examples><example_item><example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type><example_item_description /><example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[
